  "id": "DrugBank_DB11660 - MONDO_6875",
  "verbalization": "Latanoprostene Bunod is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ocular Hypertension through its association with Open-angle Glaucoma, which in turn is linked to Ocular Hypertension. The evidence suggests that Latanoprostene Bunod may influence ocular physiology in a manner that contributes to elevated intraocular pressure, potentially through mechanisms involving the regulation of aqueous humor production. The observed relationships indicate that Latanoprostene Bunod is a downstream agent in the treatment of Open-angle Glaucoma, which is a known risk factor for Ocular Hypertension. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role of Latanoprostene Bunod in the development or maintenance of Ocular Hypertension, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a causal link between Latanoprostene Bunod and Ocular Hypertension, mediated through its effects on glaucoma pathology.",
